{"sappers_hun" "A team of ten Sappers , equipped with Antitank-, Antipersonalmines and Minedetectors theese Soldiers can easily create complex minefileds against enemy infatry and Tanks and are able to remove enemey minefields, too. They bring a truck with them, fully equipped with antitank hedgehogs, barbwire and more fortifaction possibilities."}
{"home_guards(hun)" "A team of eight untrained civilians, each armed with a standard-issue FEG 35M rifle. The rifle's long range make the squad most effective over long and medium distances. However, due to the Karabin FEG 35M's low-capacity cartridge and a comparatively low rate of fire, at close range those riflemen are easy targets for submachine gunners and assault infantry."}
{"riflemans(hun)" "A squad consisting of 6 Rifleman led by a Squad leader and supported by a Machine Gunner. These Squads are most effective at long and medium ranges. In close combat, they become easy prey for enemy submachine gunners and assault squads."}
{"smgs(hun)" "A squad consisting of SMG Gunners and Semi-automatic Rifleman led by a Squad leader and supported by a Machine Gunner. These Squads are most effective at long and medium ranges. In close combat, they become easy prey for enemy submachine gunners and assault squads."}
{"mech_inf_hun" "A squad consisting of SMG Gunners, heavy SMG Gunners , Rifleman , Semi-automatic Rifleman and is led by a Squad leader.This Squad comes with an amored Troop carrier, that brings the troops fast and secure to the battlefield. These Squads are most effective at nearly every range. In close combat they are pretty good, same to medium and longer ranges.The Amored Carrier brings in extra Ammo for all infantry Weapons and carries an AT Weapon."}
{"stormtroopers(hun)" "The Hungarian assault troops were made up of physically strong, young soldiers who were given additional training before being sent on the most difficult and critical of missions, from assaulting standalone weapon emplacements to securing defence lines and permanent fortifications. This Squad consists of 8 Assault Troopers which are armed with submachine guns and light machine guns. Their arsenals also included dynamite sticks, a AT-Rifle, anti-personnel, anti-tank and smoke grenades."}
{"mgs(usa)" "A single infantryman armed with a .30 cal M1919 A6 and sandbags. Has 3 weapon skill."}
{"ammo_dude(usa)" "This boi carries a C H O N K Y amount of ammo for all the other bois other than his own chad M1 rifle. Whoever wrote this description must have been high on acid or something..."}
{"elites_82nd(usa)" "The 82nd Airborne Division was headquartered in Fort Bragg, where it became home to U.S. Army special operations units such as the Army Special Forces (Green Berets and SFOD-D (Delta Force) during the Cold War until present. The 82nd first saw their debut during the invasion of Sicily, being among the first American troops to land in Italy as they fought their way until the heart of the Reich."}
{"elites_82nd_drop(usa)" "The 82nd Airborne Division was headquartered in Fort Bragg, where it became home to U.S. Army special operations units such as the Army Special Forces (Green Berets) and SFOD-D (Delta Force) during the Cold War until present. The 82nd first saw their debut during the invasion of Sicily, being among the first American troops to land in Italy as they fought their way until the heart of the Reich."}
{"smg 2(rus_guard)" "A single skill 5 SMG soldier. Weapons:1x PPS-43. Throwables:2x F1 Grenade 1x Smoke Grenade. Consumables:5x First Aid kit."}
{"smgs2_thompson(eng)" "A single infantryman armed with a Thompson submachine gun."}
{"mgs2_can(eng)" "A Lewis machine gun team and sandbags. Soldiers are skill 5."}
{"engineers_assault(eng)" "A Heavy Sapper Section armed with satchel charges, flamethrowers and minesweepers. Soldiers are skill 5."}
{"recon(usmc)" "A team of 4 Marine recon troops in an unarmed Dodge WC-56 car, armed with 2 Thompson submachineguns and 2 M1 Garand semi-automatic rifles. Use these troops to quickly recce a portion of the battlefield or to hold points until reinforcements arrive. Soldiers are skill 5."}
{"riflemans_army(usmc)" "A squad of 12 soldiers from the US Army, including a BAR team and a grenadier. Soldiers are skill 3. These reinforcements are well used in defending locations that the Marines have captured, allowing more USMC assets to be dedicated to the offensive."}
{"rangers(usmc)" "A squad of 12 Rangers from the US Army, including 2 BAR teams, a grenadier, a sniper, and an AT team. Soldiers are skill 7. These reinforcements are very well used in defending locations that the Marines have captured, allowing more USMC assets to be dedicated to the offensive."}
{"specialinf_ft(usmc)" "A regular Marine fireteam of four consisting of two riflemen and a BAR team. Soldiers are skill 4.This mobile element can be used to provide recce or tactically surround an enemy position."}
{"specialinf_assault_ft(usmc)" "An engineer Marine fireteam of four consisting of three engineers and a flamethrower. Soldiers are skill 5. This mobile element can be used to quickly attack positions on the enemy line."}
{"specialinf_vet_ft(usmc)" "A veteran Marine fireteam of four consisting of two riflemen and a BAR team. Soldiers are skill 5."}
{"specialinf_elite_ft(usmc)" "An elite Marine fireteam of four consisting of a rifleman, a BAR team, and a rifle grenadier. Soldiers are skill 6."}
{"raiders_ft(usmc)" "A Marine Raiders fireteam of four consisting of a rifleman, a BAR team, and a rifle grenadier. Soldiers are skill 8."}
{"specialinf(usmc)" "A squad of 13 Marines, consisting of a rifle-grenadier and two BAR teams. Soldiers are skill 4. Unlike their Army brethens, all marines completed their basic in only either Parris Island or San Diego recruit depots. U.S.M.C had been known to have among the hardest training out of any branch in the U.S. military. Nicknamed 'Devil Dogs' gained from their actions in WW1, U.S. Marines are well-trained professional infantrymen. While the U.S. Army outnumbered Marine personnel in the Pacific, the Marine Corps spearheaded most of the operations as well as the island-hopping campaigns, and thus first to fight often in the Pacific theater."}
{"specialinf_vet(usmc)" "A squad of 13 marines, composed of two a rifle grenadier and two BAR teams. Soldiers are skill 5. These marine grunts had been through some shit in the field as they honed their skill and experience. Oo-rah!"}
{"specialinf_assault(usmc)" "A squad of 13 marines, composed of a rifle grenadier, three flamethrowers, and a bazooka. Soldiers are skill 5. These U.S. marines are combat engineers tasked with demolitions of obstacles and assaulting enemy positions, and thus equipped with satchel charges and M2 Flamethrowers."}
{"paramarines(usmc)" "A squad of 13 paramines, composed of a sniper, two BAR teams, a rifle grenadier, and a .30 cal. team. Soldiers are skill 6. Paramarines were meant to be used as vanguards ahead and in support of amphibious operations, to capture critical points like airfields, and conduct reconnaissance behind enemy lines. It officially ceased to exist on 29 February 1944, folded into regular marine infantry units. Ensure these battle-hardened marines kick some ass out there."}
{"raiders(usmc)" "A squad of 13 Marine Raiders, composed of a bazooka, two rifle grenadiers, 3 BAR teams, and a sniper. Soldiers are skill 8. Marine Raiders were elite units formed to conduct special amphibious light infantry warfare, to work behind the enemy lines on special operations capacity. With the changing nature of the Pacific theater from time to time and Raiders being misused as conventional infantry, Marine Raiders had been disbanded and folded into regular marine infantry units by 1944, along with Paramarines. Ensure these battle-hardened marines kick some ass out there."}
{"lvt_specialinf(usmc)" "10 Marines mounted on LVT-4 Water Buffalo Amtracs, which are amphibious transports armed with 5 machine guns for self-defense and capable of resupplying nearby marines."}
{"lvt_specialinf_vet(usmc)" "10 Seasoned Marines mounted on LVT-4 Water Buffalo Amtracs, which are amphibious transports armed with 5 machine guns for self-defense and capable of resupplying nearby marines."}
{"hero_sniper_usmc" "A team consisting of a Marine scout sniper and his spotter, deploying with a Dodge WC-56. If positioned correctly, they will be able to provide both reconnaissance and support fire effectively."}
{"hero_breachers(usmc)" "This highly lethal Marine squad consists of 3 flamethrowers, an anti-tank soldier with a bazooka, and 8 troops with satchel charges, shotguns, and Thompsons alike. Use these battle-hardened Marines to break even the toughest of lines, burning and blowing shit up all along the way."}
{"hero_lvt_usmc" "The LVT-4(A) is an amphibious vehicle used by the USMC to provide support fire during Marine assaults using its 75mm M2 gun. Armed with HE, HEAT, and WP shells, this LVT can easily support an attack on an enemy position and even fend against light vehicles."}
{"hero_satan_usmc" "The M3A1 Satan is a truly dangerous little devil, armed with a traversible flamethrower and auxiliary Browning M1919A4 machinegun. Smaller and more nimble than its larger Crocodile counterpart, the Satan is a very effective tool in burning out enemy positions quickly."}
{"hero_marine_platoon(usmc)" "This massive force consists of 27 marines, with 6 BAR teams and over a dozen seasoned riflemen included. If you are looking to conduct a large-scale assault, or are locking down a large position, these seasoned troops are the perfect fit."}
{"hero_amphibious_usmc" "This large mechanized force consists of 2 LVT-4 Water Buffalo vehicles, armed with 5 machine guns each, carrying 2 squads of regular Marines. Such a force cannot be easily reckoned with, given how much suppression it can give."}
{"hero_crocodile_usmc" "The M4A3R2 Crocodile is an M4A3 Sherman equipped with a traversible flamethrower. Sturdier than its Satan counterpart, this unit will provide a hefty amount of flames for any assault."}
{"hero_support_usmc" "This unit consists of two 57mm M1 AT guns, two M1 81mm mortars, and a .30 cal M1919A4 M2 tripod machinegun; all being perfect for locking down a recently taken position and giving support fire."}
{"hero_m4a3e8_usmc" "A M4A3E8(76)W manned by veteran Marine tank crew, thus conferring a longer range and better accuracy than its normal counterpart."}
{"hero_sherman_usmc" "This battlegroup consists of 2 M4A3 Shermans armed with AP, HE, and WP and two M5A1 Stuarts. Not for engaging other vehicles necessarily, but rather to bolster an infantry assault and provide a massive amount of support fire."}
{"hero_m7_usmc" "This unit consists of 2 M7 Priests armed with 105mm M2A1 artillery guns. They are perfect for providing suppressive artillery fire or support against light enemy emplacements."}
{"hero_pershing_usmc" "The M26 Pershing is a heavy late-war American tank armed with a 90mm M3 gun; under Marine hands, it functions as an effective response to heavy enemy vehicles and to oversee a late-stage assault."}
{"ffi(fra)" "French resistance played a major role in disrupting the efforts of German forces as well providing valuable intelligence for the Allies. People from various backgrounds scrounged whatever they could to take the fight against German occupation. This squad of 12 is best suited to defense, particularly in urban areas, due to their submachineguns and pistols. Fighters are skill 1."}
{"ffi_rifles(fra)" "Maquisards are members of the Maquis, loosely organized resistance units founded by French citizens who fled into the mountains and hills of Britanny and southern France. French resistance played a major role in disrupting the efforts of German forces as well providing valuable intelligence for the Allies. People from various backgrounds scrounged whatever they could to take the fight against German occupation. This squad of 12 comes with an MG team, and is best suited for defense. Fighters are skill 1."}
{"saboteurs(fra)" "These FFI fighters are better skilled than the others, specialized in close quarter combat and sabotage with their armament of SMGs and explosives. Consists of 10 partisans, 2 with panzerfausts. Fighters are skill 3."}
{"volunteers(fra)" "A squad of 12 French volunteers are armed with a mixture of surplus British weaponry and French guns, and includes an MG team. They are good for holding a position or providing security to a specific area. Soldiers are skill 2."}
{"riflemans_light(fra)" "2e Blindee (2nd Armored Division) under Philippe de Leclerc arrived in Normandy in late July, equipped with dominantly lend-leased American equipment. French nationalities took the fight against German forces, racing to Paris regardless of losses, to be the ones liberating the capital of their own soil. This squad comes with 10 riflemen. Soldiers are skill 4."}
{"riflemans(fra)" "2e Blindee (2nd Armored Division) under Philippe de Leclerc arrived in Normandy in late July, equipped with dominantly lend-leased American equipment. French nationalities took the fight against German forces, racing to Paris regardless of losses, to be the ones liberating the capital of their own soil. This squad comes with 11 soldiers, and includes a BAR team. Soldiers are skill 4."}
{"riflemans_mgun(fra)" "2e Blindee (2nd Armored Division) under Philippe de Leclerc arrived in Normandy in late July, equipped with dominantly lend-leased American equipment. French nationalities took the fight against German forces, racing to Paris regardless of losses, to be the ones liberating the capital of their own soil. This squad of ten includes two MG teams. Soldiers are skill 4."}
{"mech_armor_rifles(fra)" "This halftrack carries eight troops, including a .30 cal MG team, and has a bazooka in its inventory. Use this unit to provide reliable mechanized assault and counterattack."}
{"specialinf(fra)" "Light cavalry regiments of the French forces. They expanded into a mechanized regiment during the war as light armored unit, relying on mobility and fast aggressive assaults. This squad of 10 riflemen includes a rifle-grenadier. Soldiers are skill 5."}
{"specialinf_bar(fra)" "Light cavalry regiments of the French forces. They expanded into a mechanized regiment during the war as light armored unit, relying on mobility and fast aggressive assaults. This squad of 10 includes 2 BAR teams and a rifle-grenadier. Soldiers are skill 5."}
{"specialinf_mgun(fra)" "Light cavalry regiments of the French forces. They expanded into a mechanized regiment during the war as light armored unit, relying on mobility and fast aggressive assaults. This squad of 10 includes 2 .30 cal teams and a rifle grenadier. Soldiers are skill 5."}
{"elites(fra)" "These 10 French commandos served under the British command, equipped with British equipment. Includes a rifle-grenadier and an MG team. Soldiers are skill 6."}
{"elites_marine(fra)" "French Fusiliers Marins (Naval Fusiliers) are specialized naval infantry trained for combat in land and costal regions. During the Free French campaign, they fought as elite light infantry units participating in various commando operations along with other Allied troops, other than being used conventionally. This squad of 10 includes 2 BAR teams, a rifle-grenadier, and a bazooka."}
{"sas_fra(fra)" "There were foreign nationalities within the SAS, with French having a squadron. French 3th and 4th SAS were paradropped behind German lines in French soil, carrying out operations supporting Allied advance while joining forces with local resistance. This squad of ten come with a sniper, a PIAT, a rifle grenadier, and three Bren teams."}
{"sas_fra_drop(fra)" "There were foreign nationalities within the SAS, with French having a squadron. French 3th and 4th SAS were paradropped behind German lines in French soil, carrying out operations supporting Allied advance while joining forces with local resistance. This SAS squad is able to be paradropped anywhere on the map."}
{"jedburgh(fra)" "'Jeds' were special operation teams of personnel from British Special Operations Executive, the U.S. Office of Strategic Services, the Free French Bureau Central de Renseignements et d'Action. Jedburgh team was made up of one British or American Officer, a French executive officer and a NCO radio operator of any nationality. These team were to lead the local resistance forces, as a part of Operation Jedburgh. Founder of U.S. Army Special Forces used to be a Jed. This team of 3 come in a Kubelwagen and are perfect for conducting recon. Soldiers are skill 8."}
{"hero1_fra" "This is an American M8 howitzer crewed by French support crew. Use this in the early stage of the battle to ensure that you have reliable anti-tank and anti-infantry capabilities."}
{"hero4_fra" "Vive la France! This is a massive infantry unit consisting of three Jedburgh operatives and 36 French resistance fighters. Use these men to not only assault vulnerable positions, but also to create a zone of death for any occupier!"}
{"hero_fra_rifle_platoon" "This platoon of fusiliers consists of three rifle grenadiers, four BAR teams, and a overall size of 36 troops. Such a large force of infantry can surely be used to turn the tide in both offensive and defensive operations."}
{"hero6_fra" "The M4A3(105) is based on the chassis of the regular M4A3 Sherman, but comes fitted with a short-barrelled 105mm howitzer. It is capable of destroying fortified targets and softening enemy defenses from distances that greatly exceed that of than any conventional tank cannon. It is an excellent weapon for supporting our troops and can quickly reposition itself to address any new threats that might appear on the battlefield. Use it carefully and it will serve you well."}
{"panzeriv_hero_fra" "This captured Panzer IV Ausf. H is manned by a veteran French tank crew. Use the German's vehicles against them with some of the best that Free France can offer!"}
{"hero7_fra" "This call-in consists of two M4A3E8 Sherman tanks armed with 76mm cannons. When working in concert, these tanks can pose a risk to even some Axis heavy armor, or provide a long-range helping hand to infantry assaults."}
{"hero_fra_m36_elite" "This elite M38 Jackson tank destroyer can be the bane of enemy heavy armor through its 90mm gun, HVAP ammunition, and deadly tank crew."}
{"panther_hero_fra" "The Free French have lucked out in requisitioning a captured German PzKpfw V Panther Ausf. A. Use their weapons against them to assure the liberation of France!"}
{"hero10_fra" "This deadly unit consists of 2 Jacksons, two Veteran Wolverines, and one regular Wolverine tank destroyers. They are the best when used to lock down the battlefield with their lethal weaponry."}
{"eng_wasp" "A Universal Carrier with a Ronson flamethrower fitted. This vehicle is a perfect asset when you have too much of the enemy existing in one place and you want to change that situation."}
{"25_lb_smoke_8x3" "Off map battery of 8 25LB guns each firing 3 smoke shells each. Circular error probability (CEP) 35m - Time on Target 90 seconds. - To use click the 'Call 25LB Smoke Barrage' button in the bottom right once in position"}
{"hero11_usa" "The Infantry platoon consists of 3 US rifle squads."}
}
